// CROWN A5 (LENS §2.4): a handler that negates the very effect it handles
// forbids its ARMS from recursing through it (the registration-time gate)
// while its remainder's performs of that effect are the ones it absorbs —
// the negation seen through the handler's own absorption is empty, so the
// install has nothing to check. Expect NO E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h with !E { op() => resume(1) }
fn work() = op() + op()
fn main() = (work()) ~> h
